## 2026-05-04 (update 10) — Backend Modularisation

### Motivation
`app.py` had grown to 1 071 lines. Splitting it into focused modules makes each
file easier to navigate, reduces the context needed when working on a single
feature, and keeps AI-assisted edits cheaper and more accurate.

### New File Structure
```
app.py          (~74 lines)   Flask entry point only
config.py       (~110 lines)  All constants, field maps, utility functions
sheets.py       (~145 lines)  Sheets client, sheet accessors, all helpers
ai.py           (~90 lines)   Claude AI generation functions
auth.py         (~12 lines)   is_logged_in / is_admin / is_leader
routes/
  terms.py      (~290 lines)  /api/terms/* + /api/vote  (Blueprint)
  members.py    (~90 lines)   /api/members/*             (Blueprint)
  sources.py    (~45 lines)   /api/sources + /api/init   (Blueprint)
```

### Module responsibilities

| Module | Contents |
|--------|----------|
| `config.py` | `COL`, `TERMS_HEADER`, all header lists, `VALID_VOTES`, `FIELD_LABELS`, `VOTE_LABELS`, `FIELD_TO_VOTE_KEY`, `VOTE_KEY_TO_COL_KEY`, `VALID_ROLES`, `MCOL`, `normalize_translation`, `strip_tone_marks` |
| `sheets.py` | `gs_client`, `get_*_sheet()`, `write_audit()`, `next_term_id()`, `recalculate_auto_selections()`, `lookup_member()`, `ensure_headers()`, `_migrate_term_ids()` |
| `ai.py` | `generate_term_data()`, `generate_missing_translations()` |
| `auth.py` | `is_logged_in()`, `is_admin()`, `is_leader()` |
| `routes/terms.py` | 9 routes including bulk import, inline edit, voting, finalization, AI translate, audit log |
| `routes/members.py` | 5 routes for full member CRUD |
| `routes/sources.py` | GET/POST sources + Init Sheets |
| `app.py` | Flask app creation, OAuth, 5 page routes (`/`, `/login`, `/auth/google`, `/callback`, `/logout`), blueprint registration |

### No functional changes
All routes, URLs, request/response formats, sheet columns, and session
behaviour are identical to update 9. `index.cgi` (`from app import app`)
requires no changes.

### Import chain (no circular dependencies)
`config` ← `sheets` ← routes
`ai` ← routes
`auth` ← routes
`app` ← `config`, `sheets`, `auth`, all route blueprints

