## 2026-05-03 (update 2) — Dual Romanization Search + Term Code Format

### Schema (Terms sheet — 24 columns total)
Added column 24:
- **RomanizationPlain** (24) — auto-generated tone-stripped Pinyin for plain-text search
  (e.g., xiūxíng → "xiuxing"). Never entered manually; computed via `strip_tone_marks()`
  (Python `unicodedata.NFD` + ASCII encode). Generated at term creation (single + bulk),
  regenerated on Pinyin PATCH, and backfilled for all existing rows when "⚙ Init Sheets" is run.

### Term Code Format
Changed ID format from **T001** (3-digit) to **T000001** (6-digit prefix + 6 digits).
- New terms get `T000001`, `T000002`, …, `T999999`.
- `next_term_id()` handles both old and new formats when finding the max.
- Running "⚙ Init Sheets" triggers `_migrate_term_ids()` which rewrites old short IDs
  in both the Terms sheet (col 1) and Votes sheet (TermID col).

### Search Enhancement
`getFilteredSorted()` now includes `romanization_plain` in the search haystack alongside
`pinyin`. Searching "xiuxing", "xiu xing", or "xiūxíng" all match the same term.

### Pinyin Editable in Edit View
Pinyin display in the edit view header is now an inline editable `<input>` that auto-saves
on blur via `autoSaveField()`. Saving pinyin also writes updated `romanization_plain`
to the sheet (backend returns `romanization_plain` in the PATCH response, frontend syncs it
into the term object in memory).

### UI: Romanization Font Size
`.cell-py` in the vocab list increased from `0.82rem` → `0.96rem` with `line-height: 1.45`
for better readability. Chinese term remains largest; Romanization is now clearly medium.

