## 2026-05-03 — UI Overhaul, Extended Schema, Edit/Vote Redesign

### Schema (Terms sheet — 23 columns total)
Added columns 16–23 in two phases:
- **TranslationKnown** (16) — known/existing translation, votable
- **Source** (17) — foreign key to Sources sheet (SourceID)
- **TranslationFirst** (18) — auto-computed top vote-getter (>1 vote required)
- **TranslationSecond** (19) — auto-computed second vote-getter (>1 vote required)
- **TranslationOther1** (20) — member-proposed "Suggested 1", votable
- **TranslationOther2** (21) — member-proposed "Suggested 2", votable
- **LastModifiedBy** (22) — email of last user to edit any field
- **LastModifiedTime** (23) — datetime of last edit (was `LastModifiedDate`, renamed)

`ensure_headers()` is idempotent: safely adds missing columns to existing sheets
and renames `LastModifiedDate` → `LastModifiedTime` automatically.

### Schema (Members sheet — 6 columns)
Added **Name** (5) and **ShortName** (6) to existing Email|Role|AddedBy|AddedAt.

### Schema (Sources sheet — new, 4 columns)
New 4th worksheet: SourceID | SourceName | SourceType | Notes. SourceID is
auto-generated as S001, S002, etc.

### Voting & Locking
- Voting pool expanded from 3 to 6 fields: Translation1/2/3, TranslationKnown,
  TranslationOther1 (Suggested 1), TranslationOther2 (Suggested 2).
- **Lock rule:** any translation field with ≥1 vote becomes read-only in both
  backend (HTTP 409) and frontend (🔒 icon, textarea replaced with div).
- **Auto-selection:** `recalculate_auto_selections()` runs after every vote;
  writes TranslationFirst/Second to the sheet; requires strictly >1 vote.

### Role Change — Set Final
`POST /api/terms/<id>/final` now requires **leader or admin** (was admin-only).
Set Final UI is hidden from regular members.

### New API Routes
- `PATCH /api/terms/<id>` — edit any unlocked field; also updates LastModifiedBy/Time
- `GET/POST /api/sources` — list and add sources
- `GET /api/members/directory` — lightweight email→{name, short_name} lookup for
  all logged-in users (not admin-only); used by frontend for display-name resolution
- `PATCH /api/members` — extended to update name/short_name in addition to role

### List View (replaces card grid)
Sortable table with columns: Term, Romanization, First Choice, Second Choice,
Status, Source, Added date, Votes, Edit button. Default sort: timestamp descending.
Client-side filter (All/Pending/Finalized/Not Yet Voted) and multi-word search
across all translation fields.

### Edit View (per-term panel)
Opens in place of the list view when clicking any row. Key layout:
- **Top-left metadata line:** "Created by [ShortName] at [date] · Modified by [ShortName] at [date]"
- **Translation box top row:** Known | Suggested 1 | Suggested 2 (3-col)
- **Translation box bottom row:** Option 1 | Option 2 | Option 3 (3-col)
- **Compact vote UI:** no progress bars; vote count + Vote button inline with
  translation text in a flex row
- **Below box:** Source selector, editable Context/Category/Notes (auto-save on blur)
- **Set Final:** visible to leader/admin only

### Inline Editing
Translation fields use direct `<textarea>` (no pencil icon). Saving on blur via
`autoSaveField()` — skips if unchanged, handles 409 lock gracefully.
Context, Category, Notes also editable (no vote lock) via `autoSaveMeta()`.
LastModifiedBy/Time updated surgically in the DOM without full view refresh.

### Team Modal
Replaced auto-save-on-blur inputs with explicit **Edit / Save / Cancel** per row.
Admin clicks Edit → row enters edit mode with Name, ShortName, Role inputs.
Save sends single PATCH; updates `membersData` and `allDirectory` in memory.
Non-admin users see the full table read-only. Modal widened to 860px.

### Display Name Resolution
`displayName(email)` helper resolves: ShortName → Name → email.
`allDirectory` loaded from `/api/members/directory` in parallel with terms at
page load. Updated in memory when members are added, edited, or removed.

